Deliberate negative check: the generalized registration test was proven to fail when
allow-github-commits was removed from capabilities/main.json, and to pass once restored.
It compares every command in commands/mod.rs against the invoke handler, the build-time
list and the window capability, so a missed registration fails the suite rather than only
the packaged application.

Note on build identity: the installer above was produced after normalizing the line
endings of src-tauri/src/git/mod.rs to LF, which the repository's .gitattributes
requires. An earlier package (SHA-256
EF10DDB58A4A3DDA38B7EC133F9DC2395C28658D665B9BE7E91827889E3155FF) was built from the
same code before that normalization and is superseded; the source manifest fingerprints
the normalized sources this installer was built from.
